INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'd4475081-e7f2-5fe6-b56e-671a91d49bd5','Designated community','In the OAIS reference model (ISO 14721), the designated community is an identified group of potential consumers expected to be able to understand the preserved information in the form in which the archive keeps and delivers it. The archive defines this community and its assumed knowledge base, which in turn sets how much Representation Information and metadata must be retained for the content to stay understandable over time.','The designated community is the group of people an archive preserves its files for. The archive decides who they are and what they already know. This tells the archive how much extra explaining to store. A general public needs more explaining than experts do.','It gives an archive a concrete target audience, so it can decide objectively what supporting information and formats are needed to keep material intelligible for the long term.','When setting up a digital repository, staff define the designated community (for example, professional sound archivists) to decide which file formats, documentation, and metadata to preserve.','Digital Preservation',ARRAY['OAIS','Representation information','Submission information package','Preservation metadata','Consumer']::text[],ARRAY['Treating the designated community as everyone; a vague, unbounded audience makes it impossible to decide what Representation Information to keep.','Setting the community once and never revising it, even as the audience''s knowledge base changes over time.','Confusing the designated community (who must be able to understand the content) with the archive''s actual current users.']::text[],ARRAY['Writing a repository policy that names the designated community and its assumed knowledge base.','Deciding to preserve extra format documentation because the designated community is non-specialist.','Reviewing whether an obsolete file format is still understandable to the designated community.']::text[],'f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='d4475081-e7f2-5fe6-b56e-671a91d49bd5' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Designated community'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
