INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'a3200886-cb50-5b91-965d-3132614bd83b','Representation information','In the OAIS reference model, the information that maps a Data Object (a bit stream) into more meaningful concepts so it can be understood and rendered. It divides into Structure Information, which describes the format and how the bits are organised into data types, and Semantic Information, which supplies the meaning of those data elements.','Representation information is what turns a string of bits into something you can understand. It explains the file''s format and what its parts mean. Without it, a saved file is just numbers no one can read.','It keeps a preserved bit stream understandable and usable over the long term, even after the software that created it is gone, by documenting how to interpret the data.','For a preserved WAV recording, an archivist keeps its format specification (structure) and the meaning of its fields and metadata (semantics) as representation information so it can be rendered in future.','OAIS Model',ARRAY['Representation network','Structure information','Semantic information','Data object','Designated community','Preservation description information']::text[],ARRAY['Confusing representation information (how to interpret the bits) with preservation description information (the object''s history, identifiers, and fixity).','Providing only the file format (structure) and omitting the semantics needed to make the data meaningful.','Assuming today''s software will always exist, so no representation information needs to be preserved.']::text[],ARRAY['Preserving a file-format specification alongside the files that use it.','Documenting the meaning of channel and metadata fields in an audio format.','Ensuring a future user can render an obsolete format from stored representation information.']::text[],'f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='a3200886-cb50-5b91-965d-3132614bd83b' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Representation information'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'a3200886-cb50-5b91-965d-3132614bd83b','f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='a3200886-cb50-5b91-965d-3132614bd83b' AND gt.achievement_id='f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'be1709e1-4e2a-5687-9668-982c01a01cb9','Representation network','In the OAIS reference model, the complete, recursive set of Representation Information needed to fully interpret a Data Object: because each piece of Representation Information is itself recorded in a form that also needs interpreting, it points to further Representation Information, forming a network that terminates in knowledge the designated community already holds.','A representation network is the full chain of explanations needed to read a file. Each explanation may itself need explaining, so they link together. The chain stops at things the intended users already understand.','It ensures interpreting a preserved object is complete: every layer of description is itself understandable, down to a base the designated community already knows, leaving no gap that would block access.','Preserving an audio format, an archivist keeps not only its specification but also the specifications of the standards it relies on, building a representation network that bottoms out in common knowledge.','OAIS Model',ARRAY['Representation information','Structure information','Semantic information','Designated community','Data object','Preservation description information']::text[],ARRAY['Preserving one format specification but not the further standards it depends on, leaving gaps in the network.','Forgetting that each piece of representation information may itself need its own representation information.','Not defining the designated community, so it is unclear where the network can safely stop.']::text[],ARRAY['Mapping every specification an archival format depends on to check nothing is missing.','Deciding how deep to document a format based on the designated community''s existing knowledge.','Assembling the linked standards needed to render an obsolete file in future.']::text[],'f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='be1709e1-4e2a-5687-9668-982c01a01cb9' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Representation network'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'be1709e1-4e2a-5687-9668-982c01a01cb9','f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='be1709e1-4e2a-5687-9668-982c01a01cb9' AND gt.achievement_id='f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '534c0f2a-a224-5dbe-a862-74571e036097','Restoration metadata','Metadata that documents the restoration or signal-processing treatments applied to a digitised recording — such as de-clicking, de-noising, de-hiss, or level and equalisation adjustments — including the tools, parameters, and order of operations used and who applied them. It records what was changed in a processed copy so the work is transparent and distinguishable from the unaltered preservation master.','Restoration metadata records the clean-up done to a digitised recording. It lists the tools and settings used to remove clicks, hiss, or noise, and who did it. This keeps the changes clear and separate from the untouched original copy.','It keeps any restoration applied to an access or processed copy fully documented and transparent, separating the changes from the unaltered preservation master and keeping them reversible in principle.','After de-clicking and de-noising a transfer in a restoration tool, an engineer records each process, its settings, and its order as restoration metadata, and keeps the flat preservation master untouched.','Metadata',ARRAY['Process metadata','Replay metadata','Preservation master','Reversible intervention','Provenance information']::text[],ARRAY['Applying restoration directly to the preservation master instead of to a separate processed copy.','Failing to record the tools, settings, and order of processing, so the work cannot be understood or undone later.','Confusing restoration metadata (documenting later clean-up) with replay metadata (documenting how the carrier was played).']::text[],ARRAY['Logging the de-click and de-noise settings used to make an access copy.','Documenting a restoration chain so a future engineer could reproduce or reverse it.','Keeping restoration notes separate from the untouched preservation master.']::text[],'f2442389-2379-4010-8b5a-6835773b85c7'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='534c0f2a-a224-5dbe-a862-74571e036097' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Restoration metadata'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
